[Q51_2] Context: R8.1
Q: Should the DelegationCoverage witness require only that an Emergency-mode delegation be active at any point during EmergencyMode (not persisting into NormalMode), and a Normal-mode delegation be active at any point during NormalMode? (Proposed R8.1 clarification)
A: R4.2 approve. R8.1 delegations made during Emergency mode must be terminated or revoked before the beginning of Normal sstate (the first time step in Normal mode). Delegations made during Normal mode may persists cross system's mode transition until its expiration or early revocation by an administrator. Therefore, it is possible for a delegation, initiated during Normal mode, to persists into Emergency or even persists pass the Emergency mode, depending on its expiration and whether it is revoked early or not. R4.1 approve.
