[RATIONALE]:
This fix is Alloy 6 compliant because Alloy requires all function and predicate applications to use square brackets for argument lists, not parentheses, and the previous code used the incorrect delimiter for function application.

[LESSON]:
Always use square brackets for function and predicate applications in Alloy, never parentheses, even if the function definition uses parentheses in its parameter list.
