### RELEVANT LESSONS LEARNED:

Previous Lessons:
1. Alloy 6 requires all function declarations to have an explicit return type; omitting the return type causes a syntax error.
2. - Alloy 6 requires `open` statements to be at the very beginning of the model, before any comments or code lines. Preceding comments can cause syntax errors.
3. Alloy doesn't support method-like function application with arguments in all contexts; must use relational join and comprehension.
4. Alloy requires careful bracketing for multiline conditional expressions; failure to enclose such expressions causes syntax errors blocking verification.
5. Can't use arithmetic expressions like "s.t+4" directly in Alloy 6 → Must use nested calls to TO/next (ordering) to define the nth successor in Time.

