  If set comprehensions are not expressive enough, consider defining a helper relation or using predicates.

- Step 3: Update all calls to nthNext to match the new definition if necessary.

[RATIONALE]:  
This fix eliminates recursion entirely, making the function Alloy 6 compliant. It is fundamentally different from altering function application syntax, directly addressing the root cause.

[LESSON]:  
Recursive user-defined functions are not allowed in Alloy 6; always use set comprehensions, built-in ordering, or relational join/closure to express iterative concepts.

