### Q&A REUSE AND UPDATE

Before emitting ANY question, reconcile each candidate from `Verification
Interpretation` against the retrieved `RELEVANT PRIOR CLARIFICATIONS`.

Match by INTENT, not wording: a candidate is resolved if a retrieved Q&A answers
the same underlying decision — even when reworded, narrowed, or re-framed (e.g.
"strict requirement vs. diagnostic property"). Rephrasing an answered question is
NOT a new question.

Classify each candidate:
- RESOLVED — a Q&A answers it → do NOT ask; add its ID to `reused_qa_ids` and
  apply that answer as a fixed assumption.
- STALE — a Q&A answered it but the requirement/model changed so it no longer
  holds → mark that Q&A `outdated`, then ask the revised question.
- UNRESOLVED — no Q&A bears on it → only these may be asked, and only if you name
  the specific open decision and why it blocks verification.

Hard rules:
- If you reuse or keep a Q&A `confirmed`, you may NOT re-ask a question it covers.
- A confirmed Q&A settles the REQUIREMENT. If verification still fails while its
  governing requirement is confirmed, the cause is the MODEL — route it to repair
  instructions, do not turn it into a user question.

Q&A pairs are immutable: update only status; create a new pair only for an
UNRESOLVED or STALE-revised question (`provisional` until user-confirmed); mark
no-longer-applicable pairs `outdated`.

Return only:
- `reused_qa_ids`
- `updated_status`: only changed IDs (`confirmed`/`provisional`/`outdated`)
- `updated_questions`: only UNRESOLVED or STALE-revised questions

Do not return unchanged Q&A, answered or reworded-answered questions, or invented
questions.

