  This uses Alloy's cardinality operator (#) to assert that exactly one EmergencyTrigger exists, which is the intended meaning.

[RATIONALE]:
This fix is Alloy 6 compliant because it replaces an incomplete quantifier statement with a valid formula using the cardinality operator, and it is a different approach from prior attempts as it corrects the misuse of quantifiers rather than focusing only on block separation or fact modularization.

[LESSON]:
Standalone quantifiers without a body or constraint are not valid in Alloy; always use either a formula or a block to express the intended property.
